course: dictionary
lesson: 10682
title: Unplug: switching off and clearing the way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unplug is a verb, and its parts give a clue. The un- means undo, and plug is the part that fits into a socket. So to unplug something is to undo the plug, which cuts off its power. «Before touching inside a blender, switch it off and unplug it.» The sentence tells you the blender must be unplugged before you touch inside it, so unplug must mean disconnect from the power.
explain: Context can also show you a second meaning. «Old crumbs in a toaster can catch fire, so a grown-up empties the crumb tray when it is unplugged and cold.» Here unplugged means the toaster has no power, and cold tells you it is safe to touch. Always try your meaning in the sentence. Does "the toaster is switched off from the wall and safe" make sense? Yes, so you have found it.
explain: Unplug can also mean to take a break from screens. «Noah's sister once unplugged the TV in the middle of his Tekken match; he was furious.» Furious shows that pulling the plug was not a welcome surprise. Later, the family gives a five-minute warning, which is a sign that unplugging is about timing and fairness.
fact: Unplug means to pull a plug out of an electric socket, so the machine switches off.
fact: Unplug can also mean to remove something that is blocking a pipe or hole.
fact: Unplug can mean to take a break from screens and phones, for example for a screen-free day.
fact: Always pull the plug by its head, not the cord, and never touch a plug with wet hands.
fact: «Unplug a kettle before filling it, fill it only to the line and keep its cord away from the edge.»
exercise: «Before touching inside a blender, switch it off and unplug it.» What does unplug mean here? | Turn the blender up to full speed | Fill it up with water | *Pull the plug out so the blender is off and safe to touch | Put it away in a cupboard
exercise: Which is the safest way to unplug a plug? | Leave it in and cut the cord | *Pull it out by its head, not the cord | Yank it out by the cord | Pull it out with wet hands
exercise: «Old crumbs in a toaster can catch fire, so a grown-up empties the crumb tray when it is unplugged and cold.» Find and copy the word that means the toaster has no power. | toaster | *unplugged | crumbs | empties
test: «A phone or tablet battery that swells or gets very hot can catch fire, so it should be unplugged and put on a hard surface.» What should you do with a battery that gets very hot? | Keep using it until it stops working | Put it under your pillow to keep it warm | Pour water on it and leave it in bed | *Unplug it and put it on a hard surface away from things that burn
test: Families sometimes «unplug» for a screen-free day. What does unplug mean here? | To pull a plug out of a socket | To block a pipe | To break a toy by pulling it apart | *To take a break from screens and phones
exam: «Noah's sister once unplugged the TV in the middle of his match; he was furious.» What does unplugged mean here? | Painted the TV a new colour | Moved the TV into a different room | *Pulled the TV's plug out so it switched off | Cleaned the TV's screen with a soft cloth
